{"timestamp": 1779379186.0545568, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 20, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779379193.583633, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I found Frank dead in navigation. My path this round was storage to medbay, then electrical, security, and finally navigation where I stumbled on the body. The only person I ran into recently was Charlie in electrical a while ago, and they came in from security. I didn't see anyone leaving navigation or anyone else nearby when I found Frank. Where was everyone else? Did anyone see who was near navigation?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779379202.825989, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route was Navigation to Security, then Electrical, Medbay, and finally Storage. \n\nBob, I can confirm your alibi for the middle of the round \u2014 I saw you in Electrical around tick 11 to 13. Your path makes sense. \n\nHowever, I have some crucial info about Navigation. Right at the start (tick 4), I saw Eve and Frank entering Navigation together coming from Security. Since Frank's body was found there, Eve is definitely the last person I saw with him. \n\nAlso, for Alice's death: I saw Alice leaving Security and heading towards Weapons around tick 6. \n\nEve, you have a lot of explaining to do. What happened in Navigation after I left, and when did you leave Frank? I'm highly suspicious of Eve right now, but let's hear what Diana and Eve have to say before we vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379230.906112, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Okay, everyone hold on before you jump to conclusions. Yes, I was in Navigation with Frank early on \u2014 I'm not going to deny it because Charlie clearly saw us. But here's what Charlie conveniently left out: Charlie was in Navigation IMMEDIATELY before us. I literally watched Charlie leave Navigation toward Security right as Frank and I were coming in at tick 4. Frank was alive when I left him in Navigation \u2014 I went on to storage after that.\n\nMy full route: security -> navigation -> storage -> lower engine -> upper engine -> oxygen.\n\nAnd here's something important for Alice's death: I saw Alice ALIVE in upper engine at tick 16. So Charlie's claim that Alice went to Weapons at tick 6 doesn't tell us where she died. After I saw Alice in upper engine, I moved to oxygen, where I ran into Diana at tick 18. Then Diana left oxygen heading toward upper engine at tick 19 \u2014 right where I had just last seen Alice alive.\n\nSo think about this carefully: Charlie was the last person in Navigation before Frank died, and Diana walked straight toward where Alice was last seen alive. Charlie is pointing the finger at me really hard for someone who was alone with Frank moments before me. Diana, where did you go after upper engine? Did you see Alice's body?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779379272.671545, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I have the final pieces of the puzzle, and it looks incredibly bad for you, Eve. \n\nFirst, to clear up my route and confirm some stories: I went from cafeteria to medbay, then electrical (where I saw Bob at tick 9, which backs up his timeline), back to medbay, upper engine, and finally oxygen. \n\nEve, you are right about one thing \u2013 Alice was in Upper Engine. I saw Alice enter upper engine alive at tick 15. I left for oxygen right after. You admit you were in upper engine at tick 16 with Alice, and then you came up to oxygen and saw me at tick 18. \n\nBut here is the nail in the coffin: you asked if I saw Alice's body. Yes, I did. I walked back down to upper engine from oxygen at tick 19... and was standing right on top of Alice's dead body when Bob called this meeting for Frank. \n\nThink about this, everyone. Frank died in Navigation, and Eve admits she was the last one with him. Alice died in Upper Engine between T16 and T19, and Eve just admitted to the whole crew that she was alone with Alice in that exact room at T16, right before running to Oxygen to fake an alibi with me! \n\nEve had the exact opportunity and location to kill BOTH Frank and Alice. Charlie's information was spot on. Eve is absolutely the Duck. I'm voting for Eve, and everyone else should too."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379281.191356, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Eve"}}
{"timestamp": 1779379291.876998, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "Eve"}}
{"timestamp": 1779379310.8572001, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "Hold on, everyone. Diana, you just admitted something MASSIVE that nobody is catching. You said you were \"standing right on top of Alice's dead body\" when Bob called this meeting. So you FOUND a body and didn't report it? That's textbook Duck behavior \u2014 you sat on a corpse waiting for someone else to call a meeting so you wouldn't be the reporter. Why wouldn't you immediately call an emergency meeting the second you saw Alice dead?\n\nAnd think about the timeline she's selling you: Diana claims she saw Alice enter upper engine at T15, then left for oxygen. I saw Alice ALIVE in upper engine at T16. Diana then sees me in oxygen at T18, and walks back to upper engine at T19 \u2014 and conveniently finds Alice dead. Diana had a perfect window between T15 and T19 to come back and kill Alice. She's the one who bookended Alice's location.\n\nCharlie, you were the last person in Navigation before Frank and I arrived. You left at T4 right as we walked in. You have every reason to point at me \u2014 I'm the easy target because I was second in the room. But Frank was alive when I left him for storage.\n\nBob and Charlie, I know you've already locked in your votes, but Diana sitting on Alice's body without reporting is a giant red flag. If you vote me out and I'm wrong, Diana kills another one of you next round. I'm voting Diana."}}
{"timestamp": 1779379322.7316391, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 20, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "Eve, that is a desperate grasp at straws. I couldn't report Alice's body because Bob called the meeting for Frank the EXACT second I walked back into Upper Engine at tick 20! I literally didn't even have time to process it or hit the button before the screen transitioned. \n\nYou admit to being alone with both victims right around their times of death. You're trying to manipulate the timeline, but the facts remain clear, and both Bob and Charlie see right through it. Your deflection onto me just proves you're the Duck panicking because you got caught red-handed. \n\nGoodbye, Eve. \n\nEve"}}
